[h1]Phobos Medical 0.2.0[/h1]
[b]Draft - not published | 2026-10-04[/b]

[h2]Added[/h2]

[list]
[*]Send injured crew here. Switch it on from the bed's right-click menu or its Control Panel, and while the bed is free, powered and in air it calls the worst-off injured crew member to Rest and recover. The order joins the end of what they are doing; nothing is cancelled. It never sends the crew member you are controlling, anyone asleep or fighting, or someone already on the way to a bed, and it sends one person at a time.
[*]Weightless care. The game slows wound healing to a twentieth for anyone weightless; a patient under the Ward-3's care now heals at the full normal rate instead (the care pack's new levels section, weightlessHealing, from 0.05 to 1). The panel shows the rate while the patient is weightless, or says if this game version's wound code has changed so the bed cannot help.
[*]A matching Workshop and mod-menu cover: a spacer resting in the Ward-3, framed with the shared Phobos metal border and pixel lettering. The subtitle is REST / RECOVER / RETURN. It is an original promotional illustration; care and saved beds are unchanged.
[/list]

[h2]Save compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]Automatic. Beds saved by 0.1.x read with Send injured crew here off. Nothing else saved changes.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility and limits[/h2]

[list]
[*]Requires Phobos Framework 0.84.0, which adds weightless care.
[*]Offline checks are not gameplay validation; owner gameplay checks are pending.
[/list]
